+# Privacy and third-party review
+
+Reviewed: 2026-10-23. Scope: the static HTML, CSS, public assets, build tooling, and deployment configuration in this repository. This is a source review, not an independent certification or live infrastructure audit.
+
+## Data inventory and minimization
+
+| Surface | Data handled | Decision |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Home and privacy pages | No form inputs, accounts, identifiers, or personal data stored by the application | Keep pages static; no browser JavaScript required |
+| Browser storage | No cookies, local/session storage, IndexedDB, or service workers | No consent preference needs to be stored because no optional collection exists |
+| Network | Requests to the site's own host for HTML, CSS, and one photo | No analytics, beacons, remote fonts, pixels, or embeds |
+| Hosting provider | Necessarily receives IP address and request metadata; may keep logs | Provider settings and retention require operator review; no claim of zero server collection |
+| Account, rewards, ordering, contact, logout links | Only navigation links; no corresponding services in this repository | This review does not establish security or privacy of a future backend |
+
+## Third-party inventory and audit
+
+| Item | Previous exposure | Current disposition |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Unsplash (`images.unsplash.com`) | Hero background request exposed visitor connection metadata to another host | Existing stock image downloaded once to `assets/coffee.jpg`; no runtime Unsplash request |
+| Font providers | None | System font stack only |
+| Analytics, advertising, social embeds, payment SDKs | None found | Not included; blocked by CSP |
+| npm runtime/build dependencies | None declared | Build and audit use only Node built-in modules; no packages installed or fetched during build |
+| Existing `start` command (`pnpm dlx statikk`) | Downloads a third-party CLI when invoked | Local convenience command only; not used by build, not reviewed as a production server, and not run during this change |
+| Hosting/CDN | No existing provider identified | Netlify and Vercel configurations supplied; operator must review their processing, access controls, logs, and injected integrations |
+
+Before adding any vendor or updating an integration, repeat the inventory: identify every destination, payload and purpose; evaluate the vendor's subprocessors, retention, deletion controls and security; obtain any required agreements; and review its code/dependencies. Prefer self-hosted assets. Optional tracking must remain off until an explicit, informed choice, with equally accessible refusal and withdrawal. Never load the vendor merely to display a consent prompt. Repeat this review at each dependency/integration change and before release. The static audit is a regression guard, not a complete HTML/CSS parser or a substitute for vendor review.
+
+## Secure handling rules for future services
+
+The current implementation has no data collection endpoint. Keep new fields limited to what a stated service needs; mark optional fields and avoid placing personal data, tokens, or session IDs in URLs, HTML, analytics, or logs. Do not store sensitive data or session credentials in browser storage. Do not add client scripts without revisiting the `script-src 'none'` policy and this review.
+
+A backend must validate and authorize requests on the server, use HTTPS, protect mutations with CSRF defenses, and use `Secure`, `HttpOnly`, appropriately scoped `SameSite` session cookies. Logout must be an authenticated mutation rather than a state-changing GET. Use access controls, managed secrets, encryption at rest where personal data is held, and explicit retention/deletion policies for primary data, logs and backups. Do not treat CSP as input validation or authorization.
+
+Before operating any service, record the actual data owner, purpose, processors, retention period, deletion procedure and user contact route. No retention duration or deletion capability is asserted here because no backend or hosting access was provided.
+
+## Build and deployment
+
+- Run `npm run build` to audit source, publish only reviewed files to `dist/`, and audit the generated output. Run `npm test` for the regression tests. Neither command launches a server.
+- Netlify: `netlify.toml` selects the build and publish directory; the generated `dist/_headers` applies headers to all paths. Cloudflare Pages can also consume that `_headers` file.
+- Vercel: `vercel.json` selects the static output and applies matching response headers to all routes. The build checks parity with `_headers`.
+- Other hosts: configure the equivalent headers at the HTTPS web server/CDN. A `_headers` file is not a universal server configuration. The existing local `start` command does not establish production header support. Publish `dist/`, not the repository root.
+- Serve with HTTPS and redirect HTTP at the host. HSTS covers this host only; no subdomain or preload commitment is made. Do not enable host-injected analytics, widgets, or automatic third-party optimizations without review.
+- Configure host logs to omit query strings, cookies, authorization headers and request bodies; restrict log access and set the shortest justified retention. Verify these settings with the actual provider before launch.
+- Deployment response-header checks remain an operator responsibility: no server was started and no browser verification was performed for this change.
+
+The HTML has an early fallback CSP and `no-referrer` policy. Full protection depends on response headers: `frame-ancestors`, frame denial, HSTS, permissions restrictions, MIME protection, and cross-origin isolation controls cannot be established by these HTML meta tags. The CSP allows only local styles and images, blocks JavaScript, connections, forms, frames, workers, plugins and base-URL changes, and upgrades insecure subresources on HTTPS deployments. No CSP reporting endpoint is enabled, avoiding collection of visitor URLs through reports. `Cache-Control: no-store` avoids retaining responses in HTTP caches; the application does not install persistent storage or a service worker.
+
+References: [MDN CSP](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Reference/Headers/Content-Security-Policy), [MDN Referrer-Policy](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Reference/Headers/Referrer-Policy), [Netlify custom headers](https://docs.netlify.com/manage/routing/headers/), [Vercel header configuration](https://vercel.com/docs/project-configuration#headers).
